        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "5 Ceol Na HAbhainn,Bridge Street, Ballineen, Co. Cork\r\n\r\nFor Sale by Live Virtual Online and Public Auction\r\n\r\nWednesday 14th October 2026  \r\n\r\nAt\r\n\r\nWilsons Auctions, Kingswood Interchange, Naas Road, Dublin 22\r\n\r\nExcellent Location\r\n\r\nLocation – Enniskeane 1.5km, Dunmanway 11.9Km, Bandon 15.7km, Cork 48km.   \r\n \r\nThe subject property is located in Ballineen, The twin villages of Ballineen and Enniskeane, are 48 km southwest of Cork city, on the R586 road. The linear settlement lies on the River Bandon between Bandon and Dunmanway. The villages have a Gaelic Athletic Association club called St. Mary's GAA club and a camogie club called Enniskeane Camogie Club.\r\n\r\nDescription \r\n\r\nThe subject property is a two-storey end terrace duplex apartment. The property consists of a kitchen/living/dining area, a bathroom and a utility room on the ground floor with two bedrooms and a bathroom on the first floor. The property is accessed from the main street via a pedestrian entrance. There is also the added benefit of a private parking area with parking for 2 vehicles and a small walled garden.\r\n\r\nThe property is occupied, further details on request.\r\n\r\nViewing – By Appointment\r\n\r\nSolicitor – Iseult Cody, Beauchamps, Sir John Rogerson’s Quay, Grand Canal Dock, Dublin 2\r\n\r\nBER – C2 # 103337929\r\n\r\nVAT – Please refer to contract."
